# Git for Windows sets core.autocrlf=true, and then it rewrites every
# file it takes for text while checking it out. The speaker model is
# held against a SHA-256 sum, so one changed line ending is enough:
# config.yaml came out as f2e36f30... instead of 5ce2bfa9..., and the
# program declared its own model broken. Measured on 24.8.2026 on a
# GitHub Windows runner, and proved by setting core.autocrlf false --
# the sum was right again and the test went green.
#
# Every Windows user who cloned this repository got that model.
models/** -text

# The same reasoning for anything else held against a checksum or read
# byte for byte.
*.png -text
*.wav -text
*.mov -text
